<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Chupas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1542</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civil-wars-between-the-conquistadors-in-peru">Civil wars between the conquistadors in Peru</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Chupas was fought on 16 September 1542 near Huamanga (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a>) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, when the royal governor Cristóbal Vaca de Castro defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro-the-younger">Diego de Almagro the Younger</a>, whose followers had murdered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> in 1541. Almagro was captured and beheaded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>, ending the Almagrist faction in the civil wars of the conquistadors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-chupas.jpg" alt="Battle of Chupas" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_chupas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
